# 🎯 Tarot System - Cursor Rules & Development Guidelines

## 📋 PROJECT OVERVIEW
Tarot Reading AI System - A modern web application for AI-powered tarot readings with personalization capabilities.

## 🏗️ TECH STACK (AGREED)
- **Frontend**: Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- **Backend**: FastAPI + Python 3.11+ + Motor (async MongoDB)
- **Database**: MongoDB Atlas (512MB free tier)
- **AI**: Ollama (Local LLM) + Groq API (fallback)
- **Deployment**: Vercel (Frontend) + Render.com (Backend)
- **Cost**: 100% FREE hosting and services

## 🎨 FRONTEND GUIDELINES

### Next.js 14 Best Practices
- Use App Router (not Pages Router)
- Implement TypeScript strictly
- Use Server Components by default, Client Components when needed
- Follow Next.js 14 file conventions:
  ```
  app/
  ├── (auth)/
  ├── api/
  ├── components/
  ├── globals.css
  ├── layout.tsx
  └── page.tsx
  ```

### Styling & UI
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Implement Shadcn/ui components
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Dark/Light theme support
- Vietnamese language support

### State Management
- Use Zustand for global state
- React Hook Form + Zod for form validation
- Local storage for session data (anonymous users)

## ⚙️ BACKEND GUIDELINES

### FastAPI Structure
```
backend/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py
│   ├── config.py
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── user.py
│   │   ├── tarot.py
│   │   └── reading.py
│   ├── api/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── v1/
│   │   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   │   ├── readings.py
│   │   │   ├── users.py
│   │   │   └── ai.py
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── database.py
│   │   ├── security.py
│   │   └── config.py
│   ├── services/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── ai_service.py
│   │   ├── tarot_service.py
│   │   └── user_service.py
│   └── utils/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       └── helpers.py
├── requirements.txt
└── Dockerfile
```

### Python Best Practices
- Use type hints everywhere
- Async/await for database operations
- Pydantic models for validation
- Environment variables for configuration
- Proper error handling and logging

## 🗄️ DATABASE DESIGN

### MongoDB Collections
1. **users** - Optional user accounts
2. **tarot_cards** - Static tarot card data
3. **readings** - Core reading data
4. **ai_training_data** - Training data collection
5. **sessions** - Anonymous user sessions

### Schema Guidelines
- Use ObjectId for _id fields
- Include created_at and updated_at timestamps
- Implement proper indexing for performance
- Follow MongoDB naming conventions

## 🤖 AI INTEGRATION

### Local LLM (Primary)
- Use Ollama for local model hosting
- Support Llama 3.1 8B and Mistral 7B models
- Implement fallback to cloud APIs
- Collect training data for personalization

### AI Service Structure
```python
class AIService:
    async def generate_reading(self, question: str, cards: List[Card]) -> str
    async def train_model(self, training_data: List[dict]) -> bool
    async def get_personalized_response(self, user_id: str, question: str) -> str
```

## 🔐 SECURITY & PRIVACY

### User Management Strategy
- **Phase 1**: Anonymous users with session tracking
- **Phase 2**: Optional user accounts (email signup)
- **Phase 3**: Full personalization with AI training

### Data Protection
- GDPR compliance for EU users
- Anonymize data after 30 days (anonymous users)
- User data export and deletion capabilities
- Secure API endpoints with rate limiting

## 🚀 DEPLOYMENT STRATEGY

### Environment Variables
```bash
# Frontend (Vercel)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=Tarot AI

# Backend (Render)
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://...
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
```

### Deployment Checklist
- [ ] Frontend deployed to Vercel
- [ ] Backend deployed to Render.com
- [ ] MongoDB Atlas connected
- [ ] Environment variables configured
- [ ] Domain and SSL setup
- [ ] Monitoring and logging

## 📊 DEVELOPMENT PHASES

### Phase 1: MVP (Weeks 1-3)
- Basic tarot card system
- Anonymous readings
- Local AI integration
- Simple UI/UX

### Phase 2: Enhancement (Weeks 4-6)
- User accounts (optional)
- Reading history
- AI personalization
- Advanced UI features

### Phase 3: Advanced Features (Weeks 7-9)
- AI model training
- Analytics dashboard
- Premium features
- Performance optimization

## 🧪 TESTING STRATEGY

### Frontend Testing
